{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Annie (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />), Bogdan (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), Cao (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), Daniel (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), and Emily (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) are running for student government positions. Their campaign posters are printed by different printing companies. The graph below plots each student’s total price of their first batch of posters versus the number of posters in their first batch.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 1 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which two students are paying the same price per poster?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a>, we know that Daniel pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c030e1eabde01498527b3c53e08763522c0c7da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> per poster and Cao pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d8fd61137f32d81435ba367a81cd8c4a9d550e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> per poster.\n</p><p>Next, we can find the price per poster for each of Annie, Bodgan, and Emily and see if any are equal to each other.\n</p><p>Using a similar process for finding the price per poster of Cao in part a, we can see that Annie pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc3719c11bac960e400f5099762d5e39f6476d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> per poster, Bogdan pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> per poster, and Emily pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> per poster.\n</p><p>Thus, the two students that pay the same price per poster are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d117eb6bedb4a7f55b9ec4f775227bc63ca26a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{Bodgan and Emily}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the graph, we can notice that the line that passes through point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> also passes through point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that the slope are equal when connecting the origin to each point.\n</p><p>In this case, the slope represents the price per poster. Thus, the two students that pay the same price per poster are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d117eb6bedb4a7f55b9ec4f775227bc63ca26a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{Bodgan and Emily}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012717\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 74/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2483/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.466      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.466      1 -total\n 39.00%    5.252      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35551:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012717 and revision id 277898. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}